Practical Explanation

After capturing each packet, the program displays useful network information.
First, it displays the packet summary.
print(packet.summary())

Then it displays the source IP address.
print(packet["IP"].src)

Next, it displays the destination IP address.
print(packet["IP"].dst)

It also displays the source and destination port numbers.
print(packet["TCP"].sport)
print(packet["TCP"].dport)

The packet size is displayed using:
print(len(packet))

If the packet contains raw data, the payload can also be displayed.
if packet.haslayer("Raw"):
    print(packet["Raw"].load)

Displaying this information helps in network monitoring, traffic analysis, troubleshooting, and understanding how data is transmitted over a network.
